    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Add or Remove a Company",
      "Anchor": "add-or-remove-a-company",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company"
      ],
      "Text": "Add or remove a single company from a DMP Segment.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "http\n\n\ncurl",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "POST https://api.linkedin.com/rest/dmpSegments/10804/companies",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "{\n    \u0022action\u0022: \u0022ADD\u0022,\n    \u0022companyName\u0022: \u0022LinkedIn\u0022,\n    \u0022companyWebsiteDomain\u0022: \u0022linkedin.com\u0022,\n    \u0022companyPageUrl\u0022: \u0022www.linkedin.com/company/linkedin\u0022,\n    \u0022stockSymbol\u0022: \u0022MSFT\u0022,\n    \u0022industries\u0022: [\n      \u0022information technology\u0022,\n      \u0022software\u0022\n    ],\n    \u0022city\u0022: \u0022Seattle\u0022,\n    \u0022state\u0022: \u0022WA\u0022,\n    \u0022country\u0022: \u0022US\u0022,\n}",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "curl -X POST \u0027https://api.linkedin.com/rest/dmpSegments/10804/companies\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027Authorization: Bearer {INSERT_TOKEN}\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027Content-Type: application/json\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027Linkedin-Version: {version number in the format YYYYMM}\u0027 \\ \n-H \u0027X-Restli-Protocol-Version: 2.0.0\u0027 \\\n--data \u0027{\n    \u0022action\u0022: \u0022ADD\u0022,\n    \u0022companyName\u0022: \u0022LinkedIn\u0022,\n    \u0022companyWebsiteDomain\u0022: \u0022linkedin.com\u0022,\n    \u0022companyPageUrl\u0022: \u0022www.linkedin.com/company/linkedin\u0022,\n    \u0022stockSymbol\u0022: \u0022MSFT\u0022,\n    \u0022industries\u0022: [\n      \u0022information technology\u0022,\n      \u0022software\u0022\n    ],\n    \u0022city\u0022: \u0022Seattle\u0022,\n    \u0022state\u0022: \u0022WA\u0022,\n    \u0022country\u0022: \u0022US\u0022,\n}\u0027",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "A successful response returns a 201 Created HTTP status code.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove a Company",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "A 201 Created HTTP status code is returned if you add the same ID again or remove an already deleted ID. This is by design.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
      "Anchor": "add-or-remove-multiple-companies",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies"
      ],
      "Text": "Add or remove multiple companies from a DMP Segment by passing the X-RestLi-Method: BATCH_CREATE header. This method is more efficient than sending individual requests to add or remove companies. Stream up to 5000 companies in a single batch request. If you see issues with your batch request responses, try to resubmit with smaller batch size.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "http\n\n\ncurl",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "POST https://api.linkedin.com/rest/dmpSegments/10804/companies",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "{\n   \u0022elements\u0022: [\n       {\n            \u0022action\u0022: \u0022ADD\u0022,\n            \u0022companyName\u0022: \u0022LinkedIn\u0022\n       },\n       {\n            \u0022action\u0022: \u0022ADD\u0022,\n            \u0022companyName\u0022: \u0022Microsoft\u0022\n       }\n   ]\n}",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "curl -X POST \u0027https://api.linkedin.com/rest/dmpSegments/10804/companies\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027X-RestLi-Method: BATCH_CREATE\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027Authorization: Bearer {INSERT_TOKEN}\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027Content-Type: application/json\u0027 \\\n-H \u0027Linkedin-Version: {version number in the format YYYYMM}\u0027 \\ \n-H \u0027X-Restli-Protocol-Version: 2.0.0\u0027 \\\n--data \u0027{\n   \u0022elements\u0022: [\n       {\n            \u0022action\u0022: \u0022ADD\u0022,\n            \u0022companyName\u0022: \u0022LinkedIn\u0022\n       },\n       {\n            \u0022action\u0022: \u0022ADD\u0022,\n            \u0022companyName\u0022: \u0022Microsoft\u0022\n       }\n   ]\n}\u0027",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "A 400 Bad Request is returned if the request syntax is incorrect. For valid syntax, we return a batch response array with HTTP response status for each element, including 201 status for success and 400 status for errors. If there\u0027s an error, the message field will reference the batchIndex, specifying the exact index of the invalid element that caused the error.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Sample Request",
      "Anchor": "sample-request-1",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Add or Remove Multiple Companies",
        "Sample Request"
      ],
      "Text": "{\n\u0022elements\u0022:\n  [ \n    {\n\t    \u0022status\u201D:201\n    },\n    {\n        \u0022status\u0022:201\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Rate Limits",
      "Anchor": "rate-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Rate Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "We have introduced a 1 minute rate limit per user (member) for our DMP streaming APIs Users \u0026 Companies to prevent abuse, ensure service stability, and consistent API availability. These limits are enforced in addition to your existing daily limits per user and per app, which can be found in the Developer Portal \u003E My Apps \u003E App \u003E Analytics \u003E Quotas and usage.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Rate Limits",
      "Anchor": "rate-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Rate Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "For the /companies endpoint, an application will have a 1 minute limit of 300 requests per user. This means an application can make up to 300 requests per user within a minute.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Rate Limits",
      "Anchor": "rate-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Rate Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "If your application calls /dmpSegments/users or /dmpSegments/companies too frequently, you may get an HTTP 429 response, indicating that you have exceeded the rate limits.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Rate Limits",
      "Anchor": "rate-limits",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Rate Limits"
      ],
      "Text": "If your application performs a high volume of automated data pushes, frequent throttling may occur. While this could impact API call throughput, it won\u0027t affect the matched audience processing SLA.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    }
  ]
}
